  "query_preview": "..\n(Friday through Monday)\nIssued at 130 AM CDT Tue Oct 13 2026\n\nThe aforementioned cold front will bring a high confidence \n(60-80%) chance of temperatures remaining below 60F on Friday \nacross areas from northwestern to central Oklahoma. Across \nsouthern and southeastern Oklahoma and western north Texas, there \nis a 20-30% chance of temperatures staying below 60F on Friday. \n\nBy Saturday, daytime temperatures will rebound slightly as the \ncold air advection weakens under clear skies. Mostly clear skies \nwill help overnight lows Friday into Saturday morning to get down \ninto the 40s across most locations, and into the upper 30s in \nnorthwestern Oklahoma. There is high confidence in dry conditions \nthrough the remainder of the weekend and into next week, with a \nsteady warming trend into early next week. By Monday, highs will \nlikely get back into the 70s across the entire area. \n\nBunker",
